+
+## Surface (dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+Documented capabilities, as migrated:
+
+- **History navigation** — ArrowUp/ArrowDown over recently sent prompts in
+  the DSH composer; ArrowUp walks older entries, ArrowDown newer, and
+  ArrowDown past the newest restores the in-progress draft.
+- **Persistence** — `localStorage` FIFO store, 500 entries, deduplicated,
+  shared across sessions; quota/storage failures degrade to memory.
+- **Dock entry** — the `conversation.composer.dock` list slot (id
+  `bench-history-dock`, order 100) mounts the invisible anchor. Collection
+  reads the current Chat target through the `useChat` standard prop:
+  `ChatSnapshot.order` + `ChatSnapshot.nodes.get()`, taking the latest
+  `user`/`steering` node's text blocks.
+- **Apply-level keydown listener** — the document listener lives in
+  `apply()`, not in the dock component, so navigation survives hero/blank
+  mode where the session-scoped dock is suppressed. It stays in the bubble
+  phase and defers to any earlier consumer through `event.defaultPrevented`
+  (the shell composer keymap consumes an arrow an open slash/@ trigger menu
+  takes), then consumes a handled arrow with `preventDefault`.
+- **Input write** — `ctx.conversation.input.for(actx).setDraft(text)` (the
+  public per-session input facade) replaces the textarea native-setter path;
+  the same facade's `state` store supplies `draft`/`phase`.
+- **Arbitration and guards** — an arrow the shell composer keymap already
+  consumed (an open slash/@ trigger menu) keeps its handling; non-`plain`
+  input phases are left alone; IME composition events pass through;
+  ArrowUp/ArrowDown only fire at the first/last visual line, measured on the
+  contenteditable selection with the Range API.
+- **Bundle layer** — `cordis.patch.yml` inserts the plugin row with
+  `capacity: 500` (composition, not a host source patch).
+- **Client module** — `exports["./client"]` is the self-contained module-table
+  bundle: `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id: '@bench/dsh-bench-history-dock',
+  factory })` registers under the package name, which client-modules asserts
+  (a bundle that loads without registering its row id fails the boot).
+
+## Install (dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+The package is a self-contained profile bundle: `dsh.bundle.patch` points at
+`cordis.patch.yml`, which inserts the plugin row. Install it through the one
+official profile path — a package name, git spec, or directory added to the
+profile's `dsh.profile.bundles` layer stack:
+
+```
+dsh plugin --profile web add <package|git|dir>
+```
+
+The row then takes effect with the bundle layer (restart the web host for a
+bundle-layer change).
